# (Arabic diacritizer model is now COMMITTED — the permissive silver-only build, 15 MB, CPU-fine: it ships in
#  every distribution so it's part of the tested product, not an optional dev stand-in. Provenance in the module.)
tools/fa-restoration/__pycache__/

# Python training env (BiLSTM taggers) — not shipped
.venv/
__pycache__/

# fp32 intermediate from the English G2P trainer (EN_PRODUCTION); only the int8-quantised model is shipped
src/languages/english/en-g2p-tagger.onnx

# fp32 intermediate from the French G2P trainer (FR_PRODUCTION); only the int8-quantised model is shipped
src/languages/french/fr-g2p-tagger.onnx
src/languages/danish/da-g2p-tagger.onnx

# Sindhi tagger: checkpoints + fp32 intermediate (only the int8 model ships), and the regeneratable
# training artifacts. The MINED gold (sd.crossscript.tsv, sd.openlex*.tsv) IS committed — it is the
# input the lexicon and model derive from. sd_deva_pairs.json / sd_airab.json are rebuilt from the
# upstream dataset by extract_sd_openlex.py.
tools/sindhi/*.pt
tools/sindhi/sd-g2p-tagger.onnx
tools/sindhi/sd-g2p-tagger.int8.onnx
tools/sindhi/sd-g2p-tagger.meta.json
tools/sindhi/sd_tagger_data*.tsv
tools/sindhi/sd_tagger_meta*.json
tools/sindhi/sd_deva_pairs.json
tools/sindhi/sd_airab.json

# Scratch notes — session handoffs and working files, never committed.
*.scratch.md
